#[doc = " @brief Scrolls to the specified index.\n When smooth animation is enabled, all items being scrolled through will be loaded and layout calculated. This may\n cause performance issues when a large number of items are loaded.\\n\n\n **Format of the {@link ArkUI_AttributeItem} parameter for setting the attribute:**\n <ul>\n <li>.value[0].i32: index of the target element to scroll to in the current container.</li>\n <li>.value[1]?.i32: whether to enable animation when scrolling to the specified index. Value 1 indicates enable\n and value 0 indicates disable. Default value: 0.</li>\n <li>.value[2]?.i32: alignment of the element scrolled to with respect to the current container. The parameter\n type is {@link ArkUI_ScrollAlignment}. Default value: ARKUI_SCROLL_ALIGNMENT_START.</li>\n <li>.value[3]?.f32: additional offset. Default value: 0, unit: vp.</li>\n </ul>\n\n @ingroup Scrollable Container Component\n @since 26.0.0"]
